      "math_academy_id": "q-68552",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "At a convenience store, a $5$-pound canister of licorice candy costs $$11.20.$ What's the unit price per ounce?\n\nAssume that there are $16$ ounces in one pound.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we convert from pounds to ounces. There are $16$ ounces in each pound, so we multiply the number of pounds  by $16:$  \n\n$$\n5\\times 16=80\n$$\n\nSo, $5$ pounds is the same as $80$ ounces. Now, to find the unit price per ounce, we divide the total price by $80:$  \n\n$$\n11.20÷80=0.14\n$$\n\nTherefore, the licorice candy costs $$0.14$ per ounce.",
